+/* FEX (fex6): in the preamble, loads go first.
+ *
+ * The preamble runs once per draw as a single wave and the draw's pixel
+ * waves wait for it, so nothing hides its memory latency. First every load
+ * into a register (they only depend on immediates), so the first (sy) wait
+ * covers all of them; only when all of the block's register loads fit at
+ * once (as in ir3_sched) and the load needs no nops or sync of its own.
+ * Then, once that wait has been scheduled, the ldc.k
+ * const pushes with their a1.x writes, early enough that their memory time
+ * overlaps the ALU work instead of adding a wait at the end. In the early
+ * preamble each a1.x write and read needs an (ss) sync, so a few other
+ * instructions are placed between them when there are any.
