+/* FEX (fex6): in the preamble, issue loads as early as possible.
+ *
+ * The preamble runs once per draw as a single wave, ahead of the draw's
+ * pixel waves, so nothing hides its memory latency: every (sy) wait is a
+ * full round trip the whole draw waits for. The usual heuristics place
+ * loads late (they add live values) and the ldc.k UBO pushes last (no
+ * consumers), which gives a chain of separate waits. Here the ldc.k pushes
